# Golden snapshot files must stay LF-terminated on every platform.
# Without this, Git on Windows (default core.autocrlf=true) converts
# LF -> CRLF at checkout, and the byte-equality comparison in
# golden_test.go fails against the LF-only output of Headless.Snapshot()
# even though the rendered cells are identical. The diff in CI looks
# bizarre ("got" and "want" appear visually the same) — the only
# difference is the hidden \r before each newline.
*.golden text eol=lf
